Describe something you do to keep fit and healthy
- what it is
- when you do it
- who you do it with
- why it is important to keep fit and healthy
- explain why it can help you keep fit and healthy

One of the things I do to stay fit and healthy is walking around 10,000 steps a day. It’s a simple habit, but it has made a noticeable difference in my overall health.

I usually try to reach this goal throughout the day by walking to nearby places, taking the stairs instead of the elevator, and sometimes going for an extra walk in the evening if I haven’t reached my target yet. On weekends, I might even go for a longer walk in a park to enjoy the fresh air.

Most of the time, I do this alone because it helps me relax and clear my mind after a busy day. However, I sometimes walk with my closed friends, and it’s a great chance for us to talk and spend quality time together, which I really enjoy.

I think keeping fit and healthy is very important because it helps me stay energetic and focused in my daily life. Walking regularly also improves my mood and helps me sleep better at night. Over time, I’ve noticed that I feel less tired and more productive. Even though it’s a simple activity, it has had a very positive impact on both my physical and mental well-being.
